// Photos and PDFs to calendar, family papers, household reminders, holidays and
// letters (Henri 2026-10-25). Apply as openclaw with
// `openclaw config patch --file server/home-tools.patch.json5`.
// The new tools (reminder_*, paper_*, holiday_plan) are in the `family` server, which
// only the Chief of staff has (the family group's copy leaves them out), so no tool
// policy change is needed for them. This patch only lets the Chief of staff and the
// family bot read PDFs with OpenClaw's built-in `pdf` tool: it is in no tool profile,
// and sandboxed sessions need it in the sandbox list too (default list has view_image only).
// The Chief of staff gets its own sandbox list (it replaces the global one for henri only):
// its servers, `pdf`, and `message` for the morning action buttons. The global list is left
// as it is, so no other agent gains `pdf` or `message`.
// Delegation (Henri 2026-10-25, "CoS ohjaa perhebottia"): the Chief of staff may ASK the
// family bot to post in the group with sessions_send, one way. Send-only: henri can't read
// family's history, family can't send to anyone, email/news/main are outside `allow`.
// henri is sandboxed, and the sandbox clamps session tools to spawned sessions by default,
// so henri's sandbox gets sessionToolsVisibility "all" while the gateway-wide visibility
// drops to "agent" (an agent sees only its own sessions). VERIFY on 2026.10.6 with
// `openclaw config schema` that agents.entries.*.sandbox.sessionToolsVisibility exists.
// Arrays replace on patch, so each list repeats what is live (news patch, 2026-10-25)
// plus the new entries. Check the live lists before applying.
{
  agents: {
    entries: {
      henri: {
        sandbox: { sessionToolsVisibility: "all" },
        tools: {
          alsoAllow: ["family__*", "brain__*", "desk__*", "jobs__*", "dreaming__*", "view_image", "pdf", "sessions_send"],
          sandbox: { tools: { alsoAllow: ["family__*", "brain__*", "desk__*", "jobs__*", "dreaming__*", "pdf", "message", "sessions_send"] } },
          // Was live with "sessions_send" in it; dropped so the delegation works. sessions_spawn stays denied.
          deny: ["group:runtime", "group:fs", "browser", "image_generate", "sessions_spawn", "mail__*", "familygroup__*", "jobsgroup__*", "news__*"],
          agentToAgent: { send: ["family"] },
        },
      },
      family: {
        tools: {
          alsoAllow: ["familygroup__*", "jobsgroup__*", "view_image", "pdf"],
          sandbox: { tools: { alsoAllow: ["message", "familygroup__*", "jobsgroup__*", "pdf"] } },
          agentToAgent: { send: [] },
        },
      },
    },
  },
  tools: {
    agentToAgent: { enabled: true, allow: ["henri", "family"] },
    sessions: { visibility: "agent" },
  },
}
